  "tipAllEventsTitle": "All Events feed",
  "tipAllEventsBody": "One live timeline of your app's logs, network requests, state changes, storage operations and errors, plus display and async-operation events.",
  "tipAllEventsSteps": "Type in \"Search events...\" to match messages, URL paths, actions, storage keys or tags\nToggle the \"LOG\", \"API\", \"STATE\" and \"STORE\" chips; \"ERRORS\" keeps errors and failed requests\nClick a row for details; \"Full\" or \"Tab\" saves them as an image\nPick a device, or \"All\", in the bottom bar to choose whose events show\nUse \"Oldest first\"/\"Newest first\" to flip the order and \"Auto-scroll\" to follow new events",
  "tipAllEventsTip": "\"Clear all\" here empties every page's list — Console, Network, State, Storage, Errors and the rest — not just this feed.",
  "tipNetworkTitle": "Inspect network traffic",
  "tipNetworkBody": "HTTP requests your app makes, with headers, bodies, status and duration, plus GraphQL, WebSocket and gRPC traffic and requests answered by mock rules. gRPC comes from the Android SDK only.",
  "tipNetworkSteps": "Click a request for its \"Headers\", \"Request\", \"Response\" and \"Timing\" tabs\nFilter by method, \"2xx\"/\"3xx\"/\"Errors\", or type part of a URL in \"Filter URLs...\"\nTurn on \"Also search request & response bodies\" to search inside payloads too\nPress \"Copy cURL\" in the panel for a curl command; right-click a row for \"Replay request\"\nOpen \"Protocols\" for GraphQL, WebSocket and gRPC, or \"Mock Audit\" for mocked requests",
  "tipNetworkTip": "Connectivity checks such as generate_204 and captive.apple.com stay hidden until your search matches them.",
  "tipConsoleTitle": "Console logs",
  "tipConsoleBody": "Your app's log lines as they arrive, with level, tag and time — console calls on React Native, print and debugPrint on Flutter, println on Android.",
  "tipConsoleSteps": "Toggle \"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARN\" and \"ERROR\" to show or hide each level\nType in \"Search logs...\" to match message text or tag\nClick a row for its tag, message, metadata and stack trace, when present\nKeep \"Group repeated logs\" on to fold identical back-to-back lines into one counted row\nUse \"Export logs\" to save the filtered list as \"Text (.txt)\" or \"JSON (.json)\"",
  "tipConsoleTip": "Plain console.log, print and println lines arrive as DEBUG — switch \"DEBUG\" off to keep only info, warnings and errors.",
  "tipStateTitle": "State inspector",
  "tipStateBody": "Every state change your app reports, with its action and the state before and after — Redux, Zustand, MobX and more on React Native, BLoC, Riverpod and Provider on Flutter, ViewModels on Android.",
  "tipStateSteps": "Open the \"Timeline\" tab — it lists changes from every state library; the chips in the header show or hide each one\nType in \"Filter actions...\" to match an action or store name\nClick a change, then switch between \"Diff\", \"Before\" and \"After\"\nUse \"Restore the app's state to this point\" (needs DevConnect.onStateRestore) or \"Save as snapshot\"\nOpen \"Controls\" to pin state paths, take snapshots and dispatch Redux actions",
  "tipStateTip": "\"Diff\" fills only when the SDK sends one — Redux, Zustand and MobX do; Flutter and Android don't, so compare \"Before\" and \"After\".",
  "tipStorageTitle": "App storage",
  "tipStorageBody": "Every read, write and delete on stores you wrap with the SDK — AsyncStorage, MMKV, SharedPreferences, Hive and more — plus the current keys of supported stores, editable here.",
  "tipStorageSteps": "In \"History\", pick \"READ\", \"WRITE\" or \"DELETE\", and toggle store chips like \"AS\" or \"SP\"\nType a key in \"Filter keys...\" to see every operation on it; values match too\nClick a row to see that operation's value, size, store and time\nOpen \"Key-Value\" for a store's current keys, then \"Add key\", \"Edit value\" or \"Delete key\"\nPress \"Reload\" to fetch the latest contents from the app",
  "tipStorageTip": "\"Clear all\" in \"History\" only empties this log; \"Clear all\" in \"Key-Value\" deletes every key from the app's store.",
  "tipDatabaseTitle": "SQLite databases",
  "tipDatabaseBody": "Browse and query the SQLite databases your app registers with DevConnect.registerDatabase: tables with row counts, a SQL box and a results grid.",
  "tipDatabaseSteps": "Register the database in the app with DevConnect.registerDatabase\nClick a table to preview its first 50 rows\nEdit the SQL and press \"Run\" to run your own query\nPress \"Run\" again to re-query — results don't refresh on their own\nPress \"Reload tables\" to refresh the table list and row counts",
  "tipDatabaseTip": "Sort by adding ORDER BY to the query — the column headers don't sort.",
  "tipPerformanceTitle": "Performance profiler",
  "tipPerformanceBody": "Live charts of your app's FPS, CPU, memory and network activity, plus frame times, threads, battery, thermal state, disk I/O, startup time and ANRs when the SDK reports them.",
  "tipPerformanceSteps": "Select one device in the bottom bar — with \"All\" selected, charts mix every app's samples\nRead the live \"FPS\", \"MEM\", \"CPU\" and \"SLOW\" pills in the toolbar\nHover a chart to read the exact value and how long ago it arrived\nCheck \"System Status\" for startup time, battery drain, thermal state, disk I/O and ANRs\nUse \"Capture as image\" to save the charts as a PNG, and \"Clear\" to start over",
  "tipPerformanceTip": "Hover the red badge in the FPS row for average and worst slow-frame times, plus the last five slow frames.",
  "tipLeaksTitle": "Memory leak detection",
  "tipLeaksBody": "Leak warnings from your app: steady memory growth caught automatically by all three SDKs, more than 50 active timers on React Native, and anything you send with DevConnect.reportMemoryLeak.",
  "tipLeaksSteps": "Read the red, amber and blue counts in the toolbar: critical, warning and info\nClick a row for its \"Detail\", \"Retained Size\", \"Stack Trace\" and \"Metadata\", when reported\nCheck \"Metadata\" on memory-growth rows for each sample and the total growth in MB\nReport your own finds with DevConnect.reportMemoryLeak, such as undisposed controllers or streams\nPress \"Clear\", repeat the suspect flow and watch for new warnings",
  "tipLeaksTip": "By default memory is sampled every 10 seconds; a warning needs steady growth above 20 MB, and above 40 MB it turns critical.",
  "tipBenchmarkTitle": "Benchmarks",
  "tipBenchmarkBody": "Times the code you wrap with the SDK's benchmark calls, plus the App Startup and App Background runs every SDK records on its own.",
  "tipBenchmarkSteps": "Wrap code in DevConnect.benchmarkStart and benchmarkStop — React Native starts with benchmark\nMark phases with benchmarkStep (Flutter, React Native); Android runs have no steps\nClick a run to see its \"Start\", \"End\", \"Duration\" and a waterfall of its steps\nType in \"Search benchmarks...\" to filter the list and the stats bar\nPress \"Capture as image\" to save a run's panel as a PNG",
  "tipBenchmarkTip": "The stats bar covers every listed run — search one title to get \"Min\", \"Avg\" and \"P50\" for that benchmark alone.",
  "tipErrorsTitle": "Errors",
  "tipErrorsBody": "Lists the errors your app reports: React Native JavaScript errors and console.error calls, Flutter framework and Dart errors, and Android exceptions.",
  "tipErrorsSteps": "Flutter: start the app with DevConnect.initAndRunApp — plain init installs no error hooks\nClick the \"JS\", \"Native\", \"Android\" and \"iOS\" chips to show or hide a platform\nType in \"Search errors...\" to match the message, source or stack trace\nClick an error to open its \"Message\", \"Stack Trace\" and \"Details\" tabs\nOn a React Native stack, press \"Symbolicate\" to map frames to your source through Metro",
  "tipErrorsTip": "Flutter errors carry the Android or iOS tag of the device they ran on — there's no separate Flutter chip.",
  "tipMockTitle": "Mock Server",
  "tipMockBody": "Keeps fake API responses — method, URL regex, status, headers, body and an optional delay — and installs them on the selected device, so matching requests never reach the network.",
  "tipMockSteps": "Android: add DevConnect.mockServerInterceptor() to your OkHttpClient first\nSelect one device, press \"Add rule\", fill in the fields and press \"Save changes\"\nPress \"Push all\" — later edits, switches and deletes then reach the device on their own\nFlip a rule's switch to pause it, or open it and hold \"Hold to delete\" (Undo brings it back)\nPress \"Clear device\" to remove every rule from the device and stop syncing",
  "tipMockTip": "Rules live only in DevConnect's memory — quitting loses them, but a synced device gets them back when it reconnects.",
  "tipHistoryTitle": "History",
  "tipHistoryBody": "When a device disconnects and stays away 15 seconds, its logs, network calls, state changes and storage operations stay here as a read-only session until it reconnects or DevConnect quits.",
  "tipHistorySteps": "Click a session to open its \"All\", \"Logs\", \"Network\", \"State\" and \"Storage\" tabs\nRead each tile's disconnect time and its event counts\nPress × on a tile to remove that session\nPress \"Clear All\" to empty the list",
  "tipHistoryTip": "A session disappears as soon as the same device — or any app on the same IP — reconnects, so check it before relaunching.",
  "tipDisplayTitle": "Display",
  "tipDisplayBody": "Shows what your app sends with DevConnect.display() — a name, optional preview text, a JSON value and metadata. All three SDKs have it.",
  "tipDisplaySteps": "Call DevConnect.display with a name and an optional value, preview and metadata\nScan the rows, newest first: each shows the name, preview and time\nClick a row to see its \"Preview\", \"Value\" as JSON and \"Metadata\"\nPress \"Clear all\" to empty the list",
  "tipDisplayTip": "Each call adds a new row rather than replacing the last one — reuse a name to build a timeline.",
  "tipAsyncTitle": "Async operations",
  "tipAsyncBody": "Lists the async steps your app reports with DevConnect.reportAsyncOperation() — saga effects, tasks, background jobs — with status, duration and result or error. Nothing is tracked automatically.",
  "tipAsyncSteps": "Call reportAsyncOperation with a type, a description and the status start, resolve or reject\nOn React Native, wrap a promise in trackAsync to report it from start to finish\nRead the badge color: orange started, green resolved, red rejected\nClick a row for its details, \"Result\" and \"Metadata\"\nPress \"Clear all\" to empty the list",
  "tipAsyncTip": "Give related calls the same sagaName — selecting any of them lists the whole group under \"Saga timeline\".",
  "tipLayoutTitle": "Layout inspector",
  "tipLayoutBody": "Captures the app's current screen with its element tree — Flutter widgets, React Native components or Android views — and shows each element's position, size, padding, margin and props.",
  "tipLayoutSteps": "Select the device and press \"Capture\" to grab its screen and element tree\nHover the screenshot to highlight an element; click to select it\nOr pick it in the \"Element tree\", or search with \"Find by name or value\"\nTurn on \"App elements only\" to hide library widgets (Flutter, React Native)\nRead \"Properties\" — box model, position, size and props — or press \"Copy as JSON\"",
  "tipLayoutTip": "React Native sends a screenshot only after you call DevConnect.registerScreenshot() — without it you get outlines only.",
